Shell yoyo blame and yoyo ast now print usage a shell can run, and the REPL still shows /blame and /ast. It's committed as 60b407d7, with "Part of #1127" in the title. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test all pass.

What changed
• blame (src/commands_git_review.rs): the usage text now comes from command_form(surface, "blame"), and the shell status function takes a surface argument. The REPL handler passes Repl, so dispatch.rs didn't need touching.
• ast (src/commands_ast_grep.rs): one ast_usage(surface) helper replaces the two hardcoded copies of the usage line.
• Two more ast messages were showing /ast in the shell, so I fixed them too:
  • The "takes its path via --in … Did you mean:" hint now names the verb as you'd type it on each surface.
  • The 200-line cut-off note now says "showing the first N", which reads correctly on both surfaces.
• `dispatch_sub.rs`: only the two shell call sites (plus one test) changed. rustfmt wrapped those calls and one assert, so the file grew from 2663 to 2670 lines. I pasted that count into tests/module_size.rs with the reason.
• The old one-argument parse wrappers were only used by tests, so they're now #[cfg(test)].

Tests
• New unit test blame_and_ast_usage_names_the_verb_as_typed_on_each_surface. To check it can fail, I briefly changed the ast usage back to /ast and it failed by name, then restored it in the same command.
• tests/integration.rs: the bare_blame test had been asserting the wrong shell text, so I updated it to the yoyo blame form.
• New integration test bare_ast_usage_names_yoyo_ast_not_the_repl_slash_form.

Built binary (empty temp dir, NO_COLOR, </dev/null), every exit code still 2:
• yoyo blame prints ✗ Usage: yoyo blame <file> or yoyo blame <file>:<start>-<end>
• yoyo ast prints Usage: yoyo ast <pattern> [--lang <lang>] [--in <path>]
• yoyo ast --lang prints --lang requires a value (e.g. --lang rust)
• yoyo ast $X.unwrap() . prints … Did you mean: yoyo ast <pattern> --in .

I commented on #1127, starting with the scope line: docs, lint, risk, skill, map and memories are still open.
